Build artefacts under `build/` (including `date-toto.exe` / `test_core.exe` on Windows) are gitignored. Directories stay in the repo via `build/.gitkeep` and `build/tests/.gitkeep`.

## Building on Linux

```sh
make clean && make && make test
./build/date-toto --version
```

## Building on Windows (MSYS2 UCRT64)

**Recommended:** open **MSYS2 UCRT64** from the Start menu:

```sh
pacman -S make mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc   # once
cd /path/to/date-toto
make clean && make && make test
./build/date-toto --version
```

Produces a **native Windows executable** (`build/date-toto` or `build/date-toto.exe`). Runs in UCRT64, Git Bash, and CMD.

### Git Bash caveat

Git Bash can build if **`/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin` is early on `PATH`**. Otherwise `gcc --version` may work while `cc1` fails silently (DLL load order). Prefer UCRT64 shell or:

```bash
PATH="/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin:$PATH" make
```

## Linking notes

- Civil helpers (`days_from_civil`, `civil_from_days`, `date_toto_break_down`) are `static inline` in `date_toto.h` — compiled into translation units that include the header (fmt/parse and each test TU).
- Tests **do not** link `src/*.c`; they only exercise the inline civil helpers via the header.
- `main()` lives only in `src/main.c`.
- Debug binary is linked in one step from sources with `CFLAGS_DEBUG` (does not reuse release `.o` files).
